      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #40232. `try_copy_page_first_pages_batch` passes the registered host pool's raw host virtual addresses to `cudaMemcpyBatchAsync`. On platforms where `cudaDevAttrCanUseHostPointerForRegisteredMem` is 0 (the reporter hit it on WSL2/GPU paravirtualization), those addresses are not valid device-space pointers, and the copy fails asynchronously with `cudaErrorIllegalAddress` — sticky, only observed at the next synchronization point, so it presents as flaky HiCache backup failures rather than a broken D2H.\n\nThe fix queries the attribute per call inside the batch helper: when the device does not report support (or the query itself errors), the helper returns false and the caller takes the existing per-page `cudaMemcpyAsync` fallback, which translates host pointers and is verified working in the issue. On mainstream platforms where the attribute is 1, the batch fast path is unchanged. No new ops, no wheel/ABI dependency, and the fallback is the code path the kernel already ships.\n\nDesign picked after discussion on the issue: the alias-translation variant (`cudaHostGetDevicePointer` per destination) is a possible follow-up refinement for performance on attribute-0 platforms, but the fallback-first version here is the smallest safe default.\n\n## Verification\n\nCode-level only, stated plainly: this environment has no CUDA host, so the kernel was not compiled or run here; the JIT kernel builds on GPU machines and CI exercises it. The acceptance test for the fixed behavior is the reporter's standalone repro in the issue (raw host VA vs `cudaHostGetDevicePointer` alias vs `cudaHostAlloc`), where the failing configuration is exactly the one this change now routes to the fallback.\n\nSigned-off-by: Yufeng He <40085740+he-yufeng@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37001306790](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37001306790)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37001309343](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37001309343)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37001306917](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37001306917)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
